{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them","id":1114280,"title":"Real life places and the WoD take on them","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-10T14:38:05-07:00","id":1114280,"title":"Real life places and the WoD take on them","content":"i been thinking, theres many places in the world that i would like to see explored in the WoD such as Aokigahara or castle Houska. but what is your version on such places in the world of darkness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T17:35:21-07:00","id":1114323,"title":"","content":"Probably depend on the game line you wanted to focus on, I think. If it were Werewolf, I'd sort of have this temptation to make the Sea of Trees a Hakken or Beast Court caern. Not sure why, though. <br /> <br /> Incidently, Jeremy Bates has apparently written a series of horror-suspence novels subtitled &quot;World's Scariest Places&quot;, including the Suicide Forest in Japan, the Catacombs under Paris, Summit County OH, and the Island of the Dolls in Mexico City. While I own a copy of Suicide Forest, I've not had a chance to read it yet, so I can't comment on quality. <br /> <br /> Other sights I'd find interesting:<ul><li>Zvikov Castle in the Czech Republic (I still rather wish Wraith had done a Necropolis: Prague book)</li> <li>Changi Hospital in Singapore</li> <li>Barranco de Badajoz in the Canary Islands</li> <li>The so-called Bridgewater Triangle in Massachusetts and the Bennington Triangle in Vermont</li> <li>The New Jersey Pine Barrens</li> <li>The various abandoned and forgotten subway tunnels and stations in New York City</li> <li>Cinecitta Studios outside of Rome</li> <li>The Trinity test site in New Mexico</li> <li>The Museum Vrolik in Amsterdam</li> <li>Riverview Hospital in British Columbia</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T22:06:45-07:00","id":1114431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them?p=1114323#post1114323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably depend on the game line you wanted to focus on, I think. If it were Werewolf, I'd sort of have this temptation to make the Sea of Trees a Hakken or Beast Court caern. Not sure why, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is one in canon. The Cherry Phoenix Court is somewhere around Mt. Fuji, which is where the Sea of Trees is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T06:57:47-07:00","id":1114564,"title":"","content":"2nd the tunnels in N.Y. I'm not sure if it is true or not but I remember hearing that the undercity of N.Y. is almost as big as the city itself. Would be an awesome setting for Vampire for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T08:17:32-07:00","id":1114594,"title":"","content":"When I look for real world setting I look for settings that kind of fit the theme I am trying to convey in the game.<br /> <br /> 1) I chose the Twin Cities of Minneapolis and St. Paul, Minnesota because I love the vibe I get when watching Fargo the Movie and TV Show and feel that it matches the tone I want to set in my Vampire The Masquerade game. Basically kind of being seclude from the cannon and having more eerie/personal horror stories.<br /> <br /> 2) I chose Juarez for my Sabbat game because I watched the American version of the FX TV show &quot;The Bridge&quot; and found myself very disturbed and saddened about the city. Even though my game is ran in 1942, I try to throw hints to as why Juarez became the way it did now.<br /> <br /> So I basically I guess look for real cities that haven't been covered in the cannon, rather than specific monuments or anything to that extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T18:19:49-07:00","id":1114840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them?p=1114564#post1114564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd the tunnels in N.Y. I'm not sure if it is true or not but I remember hearing that the undercity of N.Y. is almost as big as the city itself. Would be an awesome setting for Vampire for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can find a copy, read <i>Reliquary</i> by Douglas Preston and Lincoln Child. It's a sequel to their novel <i>Relic</i> (which was made into a decent enough film), and involves a lot of stuff about the world below New York City's streets, including places where it goes down a mile or so to the bedrock (where there are supposedly natural tunnels going even deeper). <br /> <br /> I've long lamented that there was never a &quot;World of Darkness: Underground&quot; book back in the day, talking about settings and chronicles set in sewers and subways, old cave systems, mines and the like. With the existence of the Nosferatu, Black Spiral Dancers, Sluagh and other things, it seems like a no brainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T19:34:24-07:00","id":1114868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them?p=1114840#post1114840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you can find a copy, read <i>Reliquary</i> by Douglas Preston and Lincoln Child. It's a sequel to their novel <i>Relic</i> (which was made into a decent enough film), and involves a lot of stuff about the world below New York City's streets, including places where it goes down a mile or so to the bedrock (where there are supposedly natural tunnels going even deeper). <br /> <br /> I've long lamented that there was never a &amp;quot;World of Darkness: Underground&amp;quot; book back in the day, talking about settings and chronicles set in sewers and subways, old cave systems, mines and the like. With the existence of the Nosferatu, Black Spiral Dancers, Sluagh and other things, it seems like a no brainer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! I loved both of those books. <br /> <br /> On a related note I feel like the creatures from the film The Descent would make one hell of a revenant family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T18:56:01-07:00","id":1115330,"title":"","content":"I think it's a shame White Wolf used the Winchester Mystery House as a vampire's haven; if anything in America screams Wraith, it's that house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T14:24:04-07:00","id":1115671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silent Witness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them?p=1114868#post1114868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes! I loved both of those books.<br /> <br /> On a related note I feel like the creatures from the film The Descent would make one hell of a revenant family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Or some sort of fomori breed. Or maybe what happens to some BSD kinfolk. <br /> <br /> A lot of stuff like that can work in different ways for each game line, which is why I always wanted a WoD book that had a &quot;here are three things this <i>could</i> be&quot; set up, so even if your players have read the book, they still won't know. <br /> <br /> I was once told that the &quot;Urban Legends&quot; book for Hunter supposedly originated with someone's pitch for a WoD: Urban Legends book that would be like a modern Bygone Bestiary, listing all these things like albino sewer alligators, UFOs, the Hook and what not, which each one having multiple answers for what it could be (the Hook as a Nosferatu leather face, a gore-hound fomori, chimera and so on, for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T13:04:35-07:00","id":1116075,"title":"","content":"I had no idea how badly I was missing a WoD: Urban Legends book until now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T08:57:18-07:00","id":1116420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them?p=1115330#post1115330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a shame White Wolf used the Winchester Mystery House as a vampire's haven; if anything in America screams Wraith, it's that house.</div> </div> </div> </div>It showed up as a Haunt and as part of the backstory for some Artifacts (The Bastard's Guns) in a Mage game I ran awhile ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T09:02:21-07:00","id":1116424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silent Witness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them?p=1116075#post1116075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had no idea how badly I was missing a WoD: Urban Legends book until now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fairly useful across the various splats (except for the typical exception of Wraith). There were a few Hunter books that were really useful overall. The Walking Dead book wasn't bad either as it really provided a whole &quot;zombie&quot; option for the game that was absent elsewhere. And First Contact was a sort of effective across the board update for all those &quot;mortals poking at the supernatural&quot; organizations from the various lines (The Arcanum from Mage, the F.B.I. from Werewolf, the Orphic Circle from Wraith &lt;shudder on that one&gt;, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T18:58:56-07:00","id":1116631,"title":"","content":"I was always mildly disappointed that there wasn't a Hunter: Against the Law book that looked at the fact that monster hunting requires a lot of activities that are usually illegal, how city and country law enforcement works in the WoD from a PC and ST perspective, and what happens when characters run up against the police in the course of their actions, as well as a look at how the FBI and other such groups would see the Imbued and be a potential threat to them. But then I was also disappointed that Hunter: Holy War wasn't about everyday Imbued who have religious and faith based motivations, religion in the WoD from the &quot;common man&quot; point of view, and what the Inquisition thinks of the Imbued. Also, Hunter: Conspiracies, Hunter: Goblins, Hunter: The Human Monster, \u2026.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:09:40-07:00","id":1118329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChristopherZacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them?p=1114594#post1114594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I chose Juarez for my Sabbat game because I watched the American version of the FX TV show &quot;The Bridge&quot; and found myself very disturbed and saddened about the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, cheer up. The Bridge's portrayal of Juarez is <a href=\"http://grantland.com/features/as-season-1-fx-bridge-winds-author-lived-juarez-takes-issue-s-portrayal-border/\" target=\"_blank\">grossly inaccurate</a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:43:30-07:00","id":1118549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1114280-real-life-places-and-the-wod-take-on-them?p=1118329#post1118329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, cheer up. The Bridge's portrayal of Juarez is <a href=\"http://grantland.com/features/as-season-1-fx-bridge-winds-author-lived-juarez-takes-issue-s-portrayal-border/\" target=\"_blank\">grossly inaccurate</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thats good..whew. Human trafficking is such a sad fucking thing. I am reading some books on human trafficking to get ready for my next Vampire: the Masquerade and Chronicles of Darkness games, and it just saddens me too. Man, I am sure getting emo on here lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}